# Anonymous Chat Feature — Y99-Style Random Stranger Chat

Add a real-time 1-on-1 anonymous random matching chat feature to GupShupGo, similar to Y99/Omegle, where users are paired with random strangers using masked identities. The feature includes instant "Next" switching, ephemeral messages, safety tools (report/block), and a **Friend Request** flow to transition from anonymous → E2EE permanent chat.

## Two-Phase Encryption Model

> [!NOTE]
> ### Phase 1 — Anonymous Chat (Non-E2EE, Ephemeral)
> When two strangers are first matched, messages are **non-E2EE (plaintext ephemeral)**:
> - Users are masked as random aliases ("Cosmic Fox", "Purple Penguin")
> - Real identities are hidden — no profile, no phone number visible
> - Messages are stored in `/anonymous_rooms/{roomId}/messages` (plaintext)
> - Messages are ephemeral — cleaned up when either user leaves or taps "Next"
> - **Why no E2EE?** — Strangers don't have persistent identities, no pre-existing Signal PreKey bundles, and the session is throwaway
>
> ### Phase 2 — Friend Request Accepted (Full E2EE)
> If both users enjoy the conversation, either can send a **Friend Request**:
> 1. User A taps "Add Friend" → a request is sent to User B (their real userId is shared server-side, but alias is still shown until accepted)
> 2. User B sees "Stranger wants to connect!" notification in the chat → taps Accept or Decline
> 3. **On Accept:**
>    - Both users' **real profiles** (name, photo) are revealed to each other
>    - A standard **E2EE chat room** is created in `/chatRooms/{chatRoomId}` using the existing `ChatService`
>    - Signal Protocol session is established via `SignalService` (PreKey bundle exchange)
>    - The new contact appears in both users' **Gup (main chat) tab**
>    - **All future messages are 100% End-to-End Encrypted** via `libsignal_protocol_dart`
>    - The anonymous room is ended and cleaned up
> 4. **On Decline:** Nothing changes — anonymous chat continues as-is

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Safety & Moderation Compliance:**
> Apple App Store and Google Play require strict UGC safety measures for anonymous chat. This plan includes mandatory **Report User**, **Block User**, and **End Room Cleanup** features. Messages are ephemeral (deleted when room ends).

## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> 1. **Interest Tags / Filters?** — Y99 lets users add interest tags (e.g. "music", "gaming") and matches on common interests. Do you want this in v1 or keep it simple (pure random matching)?
> 2. **Text Only or Media Too?** — Should anonymous chat support image/audio sending, or text-only for safety in v1?
> 3. **Rate Limiting?** — Should we limit how many anonymous sessions a user can start per hour/day to prevent abuse?
> 4. **Premium Gate?** — Should anonymous chat be available to all users or gated behind GupShupGo Pro?

