### UI Layer

#### [NEW] [anonymous_lobby_screen.dart](file:///e:/GupShupGo/gupshupgo/lib/screens/anonymous/anonymous_lobby_screen.dart)

Entry screen when user taps "Anonymous Chat":

- **Searching State**: Radar ripple animation (concentric expanding circles) with text "Searching for a stranger..."
- **Cancel Button**: Leaves the queue and pops back
- **Auto-Transition**: Listens to `match_queue/{userId}` — when `matchedRoomId` appears, navigates to `AnonymousChatScreen`
- **Theme**: Uses `AppThemeColors.of(context)` for light/dark support
- **Font**: `GoogleFonts.poppins` exclusively

#### [NEW] [anonymous_chat_screen.dart](file:///e:/GupShupGo/gupshupgo/lib/screens/anonymous/anonymous_chat_screen.dart)

Dedicated 1-on-1 anonymous chat UI:

- **App Bar**:
  - Title: Partner's alias (e.g. "Cosmic Fox 🦊")
  - Subtitle: "Anonymous Chat"
  - Actions:
    - 👤 **Add Friend** — Sends friend request to the stranger
    - 🔄 **Next** — Ends current room, re-enters lobby/queue
    - 🚩 **Report** — Shows report dialog, ends session
    - 🛑 **Leave** — Ends session, returns to home
- **Friend Request UI**:
  - **Sender sees**: "Friend request sent! Waiting for response..." (disabled "Add Friend" button)
  - **Receiver sees**: Banner at top — "🤝 Stranger wants to connect!" with **Accept** and **Decline** buttons
  - **On Accept**: Both users see "You are now friends! 🎉" system message → brief 2s delay → auto-navigate to the new E2EE `ChatScreen` with real profiles
  - **On Decline**: Sender sees "Friend request declined" system message → anonymous chat continues normally
- **Message List**: Real-time listener on `/anonymous_rooms/{roomId}/messages`, rendered as simple text bubbles (sent = `c.primary`, received = `c.surfaceAlt`). System messages rendered centered with muted styling.
- **Disconnect Banner**: When room `status` changes to `ended` and `endedBy != currentUser`, show "Stranger has disconnected" banner with a "Find Next Stranger" button
- **Input Bar**: Text field + send button (text-only in v1)
- **No E2EE banner**: Shows "Messages are not encrypted" subtle label (unlike regular chat's E2EE banner)
- **Theme**: Full light/dark mode support via `AppThemeColors`

